+     *
+     * WHY IN C: the errno NAME set is fixed (node builds it from a static list in
+     * node_constants.cc) but the VALUES are platform-specific — measured against
+     * real node, 47 of the 79 differ across darwin/linux/netbsd (EAGAIN is 35 on
+     * darwin and NetBSD, 11 on Linux). A hand-maintained JS table would be wrong on
+     * most targets and would need editing for every new platform. Reading THIS
+     * engine's <errno.h> through #ifdef makes it exact everywhere and
+     * maintenance-free — the same argument that put the signal table here.
+     *
+     * It lives in signals.c because that file is already patched, its init runs
+     * once at startup, and clode_global is already in hand.
